text":"grc"}},{"@objectPart":"translation","languageTerm":{"@type":"code","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"grc"}}],"physicalDescription":{"form":{"@authority":"marcform","#text":"print"},"extent":"18 v. ; 24 cm."},"abstract":{"@type":"","#text":"A complete 18-volume library consisting of more than 10,000 pages. System applies the \"learn by doing\" principle to teach Greek grammar, diction, and syntax. Each word is presented in order of occurrence in the Bible, first in Greek, then followed by a grammatical identification of the usage, a concordance, a definition, a translation of the verse, and finally the author's commentary. The work enables a person to make his own translation. This comprehensive study guide provides an excellent tool for students of Greek and New Testament interpretation, and serves as a timely aid to ministers in explaining Scripture and its application to the contemporary world. As an exegetical guide, it is indispensable. The author provides contextual understanding of the Scriptures via his knowledge in economic history, with concentrations in sociology, psychology, and philosophy -- BOOK JACKET."},"tableOfContents":"V. 1. Matthew I-VII. -- v. 2. Matthew VIII-XVIII. -- v. 3. Matthew XIX-XXVIII. -- v. 5. John 5:1-6:71. Mark 2:23-9:8. Luke 6:1-9:36. -- v. 6. Mark 9:9-10:1. Luke 9:37-15:32. John 7:1-10:42.","note":[{"@type":"statement of responsibility","#text":"by Randolph O. Yeager."},"Beginning with vol. 5, published by Pelican Pub. Co., Gretna, La.","Includes the texts of the Authorized and Greek versions and the Yeager translation."],"subject":[{"@authority":"lcsh","titleInfo":{"title":"Bible","partName":"New Testament"},"topic":"Concordances, Greek"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Greek language, Biblical"}],"classification":{"@authority":"lcc","#text":"BS2302 .Y4"},"relatedItem":[{"@type":"constituent","titleInfo":{"title":"Bible. N.T. English. Yeager. 1976"}},{"@type":"constituent","titleInfo":{"title":"Bible. N.T. English. Authorized.